%C A094846 Conjecture: Let h(D) be the class number of the quadratic field with discriminant D, then {h(A094845(n)) : n >= 4} is strictly increasing. If this is true, then a(n) = h(A094845(n+3)). - _Jianing Song_, Nov 16 2026
